36m`auto`[39m(B[m colorises only when stdout is a[K[48dterminal. (B[0;1m[36m`always`[39m(B[m emits the codes even when piped, so `ls --color=always | grep[49dfoo` sends escape sequences into grep.[K[26d[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?25h[28d[?25l[?12l[?25h[30d[?25l[?12l[?25h[33d[?25l[?12l[?25h[37d[?25l[?12l[?25h[39d[?25l[?12l[?25h[45d[?25l[?12l[?25h[47d[?25l[2;50r[50;1H[25S[1;52r[26;1HThe exercise asks for colorised output, so (B[0;1m[36m`always`[39m(B[m is right here. In a shell[27dalias, write (B[0;1m[36m`auto`[39m(B[m.[29dThe underlying behaviour — a program acting differently depending on whether its[30doutput is a terminal or a pipe — is called (B[0;1m[32m**TTY detection**[39m(B[m ((B[0;1m[36m`isatty`[39m(B[m). (B[0;1m[36m`less`[39m(B[m,[31d(B[0;1m[36m`grep`[39m(B[m and (B[0;1m[36m`git`[39m(B[m all do it. It's why piping something sometimes changes its output[32dformat seemingly at random.[34d(B[0;1m[33m### `-h` needs `-l`[36d[36m`-h`[39m(B[m produces (B[0;1m[36m`2.8M`[39m(B[m, (B[0;1m[36m`4.0K`[39m(B[m, (B[0;1m[36m`16K`[39m(B[m instead of (B[0;1m[36m`2871424`[39m(B[m and (B[0;1m[36m`4096`[39m(B[m. It only shows[37din long format, because short format prints no sizes at all.[39d(B[0;1m[33m### The colour that looked broken[41d[39m(B[mThe colour actually worked. It looked like it didn't for two reasons: copying the[42doutput to paste it strips the escape codes, and the (B[0;1m[36m`/`[39m(B[m listing is almost entirely[43ddirectories, so nearly every entry was the same blue and read as uniform.[45dColour in a terminal isn't a property of text. It's (B[0;1m[32m**ANSI escape sequences**[39m(B[m —[46dinvisible control characters embedded in the output stream, which the terminal[47dinterprets as "switch to blue now".[49dThe diagnosis, which is the transferable part:[26d[?12l[?25h[?25l[?12l[?2